{"name":"Hong Kong Mist","hex":"#948e90","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hong","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past of hang"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A foreign trading company in China."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hong"},{"term":"kong","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of four identical tiles.","A call declaring the formation of such a set."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kong"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hong Kong","blocks":[{"text":"Hong Kong is a special administrative region of China. Situated on China's southern coast just south of Shenzhen, it consists of Hong Kong Island, Kowloon, and the New Territories. With 7.5 million residents in a 1,114-square-kilometre (430 sq mi) territory, Hong Kong is the fourth-most densely populated region in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Flag_of_Hong_Kong.svg/330px-Flag_of_Hong_Kong.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hong_Kong","wikidata":"Q8646"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist","wikidata":"Q192196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sung_Wong_Toi.jpg/500px-Sung_Wong_Toi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sung_Wong_Toi.jpg/1280px-Sung_Wong_Toi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sung_Wong_Toi.jpg/500px-Sung_Wong_Toi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sung Wong Toi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASung_Wong_Toi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Hong_Kong_1868.jpg/500px-Hong_Kong_1868.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Hong_Kong_1868.jpg/1280px-Hong_Kong_1868.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Hong_Kong_1868.jpg/500px-Hong_Kong_1868.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hong Kong in 1868, photograph by John Thomson","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHong_Kong_1868.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/578a_Hong_Kong_1971_%2851321892645%29.jpg/500px-578a_Hong_Kong_1971_%2851321892645%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/578a_Hong_Kong_1971_%2851321892645%29.jpg/1280px-578a_Ho